{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LazySegmentTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/MonoidAction","preciseIdentifier":"s:10RangeTrees12MonoidActionP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MonoidAction"}]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The layout is "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/SegmentTree"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s: a perfect binary tree over the values padded to a power of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"two, in one flat array of cells. Beside each internal cell sits a pending update, applied to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that cell’s value but not yet to the cells below it. A range update applies itself to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") cells that cover the range and leaves it pending there, pushing older pending"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"updates down one level on the way so that updates reach each cell in the order they were made."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A query reads without changing the tree, composing the pending updates of the cells it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"passes through."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/MonoidAction","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" names the monoid and the updates:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["enum AddToSum: MonoidAction {","    typealias Values = Sum<Int>","    static var identity: Int { 0 }","    static func compose(_ outer: Int, _ inner: Int) -> Int { outer + inner }","    static func apply(_ update: Int, to sum: Int, count: Int) -> Int { sum + update * count }","}","","var tree = LazySegmentTree<AddToSum>([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])","tree.apply(10, in: 1 ..< 4)","tree.combined(in: 0 ..< 5)   \/\/ 45","tree[2]                      \/\/ 13"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As a collection, a lazy segment tree’s elements are the values, in order, with every update"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"applied."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/rangetrees\/lazysegmenttree"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LazySegmentTree","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:10RangeTrees15LazySegmentTreeV","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LazySegmentTree","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"LazySegmentTree.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree.swift#L31"},"title":"LazySegmentTree","modules":[{"name":"RangeTrees"}],"roleHeading":"Structure"},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree\/init()","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree\/init(_:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":tru